*** Add File:services/policy/okta_oidc_example.md
+Okta / OIDC example for M-of-N service integration
+
+1) Create an authorization server & client in Okta
+   - In Okta admin console, create an OIDC app for the M-of-N service (machine-to-machine)
+   - Add allowed audience (e.g., aegis-mofn) and note the JWKS URL
+
+2) Configure M-of-N service Helm values / env:
+   - OIDC_JWKS_URL=https://<your-okta-domain>/.well-known/jwks.json
+   - OIDC_AUDIENCE=aegis-mofn
+
+3) Approver workflow:
+   - Operators obtain tokens via client credentials flow (or have human approvers use browser flow)
+   - Approvers call /approve with Authorization: Bearer <JWT>
+   - The M-of-N service extracts 'sub' claim from JWT and records the approver identity
+
+4) Security notes:
+   - Use HTTPS and validate tokens on every request
+   - Restrict M-of-N admin APIs to an allowlist in k8s NetworkPolicy
+
